  "body": "The path kernel comes to `main`, dormant. This is the one PR from `side/path-kernel` to `main` of the plan of 2026-11-27 (#4023, `docs/decisions/4325-path-kernel-delivery.md`, rule **Side branch** of `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## What a user sees\n\nNothing changes. The default planner of each operation kind is the old planner. Each program that the app makes is the same as before this PR. The pins `switch_default_is_the_old_planner` and the recorded baselines of the old planners hold that.\n\nThe setting `CAMCRAFT_PLANNER=new` (for tests and for the work on the kernel) selects the kernel. At this head no kind is moved, so with `new` each phase-1 kind is refused by name (\"the new path planner does not plan <kind> yet\"). There is no silent fallback. The first kind (2D Pocket, PR #4328) is not in this PR.\n\n## What the PR brings\n\n- The crate `camcraft-pathkernel` (`crates/pathkernel/`). It depends only on `camcraft-geometry`; `camcraft-motion` depends on it. The maintainer approved the crate, its name and its edges (2026-11-25; record of #4024 in `RECOMMENDED.md`).\n- The stages: the region (K1), the guides (K2: rings, rows, medial line, trace, helix), the load control (K3), the order and the link with the proved approach from the air (K4), the entry and the exit (K5).\n- The law suite of the crate (K7, `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/`), the law measures on a finished toolpath, and the recorded baselines of the old planners for the 16 phase-1 kinds.\n- The converter from a kernel plan to a toolpath (`camcraft_motion::kernel_emit`). No operation calls it yet.\n- The planner switch, read in one place (`crates/app/src/operation/planner_switch.rs`).\n- Additions to `camcraft-geometry` (segment tests, arc points, a medial axis, a side offset), each with unit tests.\n- The gate lists of `xtask` and the `-p` list of `AGENTS.md` for the new crate.\n\nSub-PRs that were reviewed and merged into the side branch: #4123, #4165, #4167, #4175, #4181, #4189, #4193, #4234, #4244, #4253, #4265, #4275, #4279, and the syncs #4112 and #4375.\n\n## Open items (they do not block this PR; each one must be closed before the switch of a kind that it touches)\n\n- #4260: over-limit moves with no name on the stock edge line (Outside).\n- #4272: an approach from the air can meet fresh stock at full width, and no stage reads it.\n- #4300: a stay link along the air crosses the arc lead of the first entry (Outside).\n- #4236: the later stages do not accept the chain region of a trace.\n\n## Gates\n\n- Each sub-PR had its own review and its gate against the side branch.\n- The sync PR #4375 (`main` at `a5e993538` merged into the side branch): the batch gate on its head, 1234 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, with clippy and the `example_catalog*` suites; the light lane, 7 steps; the xtask tests.\n- For this PR, on the tree of this head merged with `main`: the batch gate, the heavy `motion` and `app` steps and the `example_catalog*` suites. The results follow in a comment. The PR does not merge before they are green and an independent review is clean on the head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and macOS were not built by the kernel work.\n- No operation runs on the kernel in this PR, so no posted program comes from it.\n\n## New top-level test binaries\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/kernel_laws.rs`: a new top-level test binary (rule **New tests join a directory suite**). Reason: no existing directory suite of `camcraft-motion` covers all 16 phase-1 kinds, and the law readings of each kind and of the kernel stages must be one suite that the switch of each kind extends (decision `docs/decisions/4154-law-measures.md`).\n\n## Merge\n\nThe coordinator session merges this PR with a merge commit and without `--delete-branch` (maintainer, question dialog, 2026-11-27), when the review and the gates are clean. `side/path-kernel` stays for the next kernel steps.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none (no behaviour changes for a user while each default is the old planner; each switch PR has its own row).\n\nRefs #4023\nRefs #4055\nRefs #4025\nRefs #4176\nRefs #4026\nRefs #4177\nRefs #4178\nRefs #4027\nRefs #4153\nRefs #4154\nRefs #4241\nRefs #4254\nRefs #4269\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
